      <p>Solar Gard window film Philadelphia is an Eastman Performance Films brand installed across Center City, University City, Old City, Passyunk Avenue, Northeast Philadelphia, and South Philadelphia commercial and residential properties — including Class A office towers on Market Street and Broad Street, University City medical centers and university campuses, Northeast Philadelphia K-12 schools, Old City retail storefronts, and South Philadelphia rowhomes — using the Panorama spectrally selective solar control series, Sentinel Plus energy-saving film, ArmorCoat safety and blast mitigation series (4-14 mil, ASTM F1642), and Hilite glare control film, all with NFRC-certified ratings for VLT, SHGC, and U-value.</p>
      <dl>
        <dt>What is Solar Gard window film in Philadelphia?</dt>
        <dd>An Eastman Performance Films brand with spectrally selective solar control (Panorama), energy-saving insulating (Sentinel Plus), safety and blast mitigation (ArmorCoat), and glare control (Hilite) series — installed on Philadelphia commercial and residential glass by authorized dealers.</dd>
        <dt>How does Solar Gard Panorama work?</dt>
        <dd>Uses a non-metallic spectrally selective coating to reject near-infrared solar heat while transmitting visible light — up to 77% solar energy rejection without a heavily tinted or reflective appearance.</dd>
        <dt>What Solar Gard products are available in Philadelphia?</dt>
        <dd>Panorama solar control (VLT 25-70%, up to 77% heat rejection), Sentinel Plus (energy-saving, NFRC), ArmorCoat (4-14 mil, ASTM F1642), Hilite (glare control, VLT 35-55%).</dd>
        <dt>Which Philadelphia buildings use Solar Gard window film?</dt>
        <dd>Center City Class A offices, University City healthcare and academic facilities, Northeast Philadelphia schools, Old City retail storefronts, Passyunk Avenue restaurants, and South Philadelphia rowhomes.</dd>
        <dt>Is Solar Gard worth it for Philadelphia winters?</dt>
        <dd>Sentinel Plus provides low-emissivity performance that reduces winter heat loss, particularly valuable for Philadelphia commercial buildings with aging glass and healthcare facilities with year-round energy reporting requirements.</dd>
        <dt>How much does Solar Gard window film cost in Philadelphia?</dt>
        <dd>Cost depends on film series, glass area, building access, documentation requirements, and installation scope. Contact us for a free assessment and written proposal.</dd>
      </dl>
